---

### ✅ What was added

A **prominent red "＋ Save" pill button** is now permanently injected into the **top-right corner of every pin thumbnail** in the search grid — no hovering or clicking into the pin required.

---

### 🎨 Button design
| Property | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Color** | Pinterest red (`#e60023`) — matches the platform's branding |
| **Position** | Top-right corner of the image, always visible |
| **Shape** | Rounded pill with a subtle drop shadow |
| **Hover** | Darkens to `#ad081b` and scales up slightly |
| **Click** | Briefly shows **✓ Saved!** in green, then opens Pinterest's native board-picker dialog in a new tab |

---

### ⚡ How it works
1. **Always visible** — no hover state needed; the button sits on top of every thumbnail at all times.
2. **One click** — clicking immediately triggers Pinterest's `/pin/{id}/save/` flow where you pick your board.
3. **Persistent** — the rule re-applies automatically as new pins lazy-load into the grid.
4. **Non-destructive** — the button is injected once per card (idempotent) and won't duplicate on re-renders.

> **Note:** Since you're currently browsing as a guest, Pinterest's save flow will prompt you to log in. Once logged in, the board picker will appear normally.

